WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.840
Aid workers in Poland say the crisis on the&nbsp;
European Union's external border with Belarus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.880
is not over yet. Poland plans to build&nbsp;
a wall to replace the razor-wire fence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.480
between the two countries. Its aim is stop&nbsp;
illegal crossings by undocumented migrants.&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:22.960
But environmental campaigners say a wall will&nbsp;
also stop wildlife from roaming free in the area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:29.840
and could have a dire impact. DW correspondent&nbsp;
Jack Parrock sent us this report from that border&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:38.480
Residents of the ancient Białowieża forest&nbsp;
- this lynx, and these wolves - caught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.840
on camera traps earlier this year.
This 600 year old forest is home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:50.560
an estimated 12 thousand species of wildlife.
Krzysztof Schmidt studies these animals - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:56.320
he says the government's plan to build a 186&nbsp;
kilometer wall, 5 and a half meters high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.600
on the country's border with Belarus will&nbsp;
have a devastating effect on the genetic mix.&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.960
"From the moment when the wall will be fully&nbsp;
constructed, then we will have two different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.960
populations completely separated from each other.&nbsp;
And it will affect the future, it will affect the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.240
sustainability of these populations because if&nbsp;
we divide populations into smaller and smaller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.840
sub-populations, then the survival&nbsp;
is more and more vulnerable."&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:32.960
He warns forest is already divided for animals&nbsp;
by roads and intersected by multiple rail lines.&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:39.120
The government wants the wall to keep out asylum&nbsp;
seekers who were crossing the border - pushed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.440
the government of neighboring Belarus.
"I've been reporting on the issues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.920
on the border for a number of months now and&nbsp;
this is the closest I've been able to get to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:54.240
the border. Just over there, maybe 300 meters&nbsp;
away is the border fence. And the border guards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.720
say that while the numbers have continued&nbsp;
to drop, the numbers of people crossing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.520
there are still attempts to break down the razor&nbsp;
wire fences and to get people into Poland."&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:09.760
Border guards intercepted 32 thousand&nbsp;
people in November last year - now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.400
there's just a handful per day.
People in this area continue their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.863
usual winter activities while the heavily guarded&nbsp;
exclusion zone remains in place here - authorities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.863 --> 00:02:22.480
check every car which nears the border.
The government says the building of the wall is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:29.280
happening in consultation with wildlife experts.
"I'm aware that there are places in the national&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.720
park, the Białowieża forest, which need&nbsp;
special consideration. Looking at the details,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.720
I'm sure that the border guards who are&nbsp;
completely responsible for building the wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.960
they are tasked to build the wall with&nbsp;
consideration of the natural environment."&nbsp;

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.720
Back in the forest, Krzysztof says his institute&nbsp;
has provided the government with a plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.840
for wildlife pathways through the wall to prevent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:03.840
the division of animal populations&nbsp;
- and hopes it will be followed.

